<!--
  RMS MODEL SCANNER - ANALYTICS SITE PROJECT
  ================================================================================================
  An ASP.NET Web Application targeting the .NET Framework, because ASP.NET Web Forms is a framework
  that ships with it and the interface this replaces was built that way. Porting the site to a newer
  runtime would mean rebuilding the one layer of this stack that has no logic in it, and spending the
  effort where mistakes are least likely.

  The SQLite provider is referenced as a package rather than as a checked-in binary. That is how the
  native library reaches the output directory in the right shape for the platform, and it is why the
  deployer's framework build runs a restore: a package reference that was never restored resolves
  against whichever version happens to be cached on the machine doing the build.

  The client script under Scripts/ is generated by the Node package under Client/, which the deployer
  builds before this project. It is committed as well, so the site still runs from a checkout that has
  never had npm installed.
-->
